// Generated by CRM App/sync/build_scripts.py from the vault call scripts. Don't edit by hand.
window.AWD_SCRIPTS = {"A": "<p><i>v2.1, 2026-10-08 (letter follow-up gatekeeper opener). v2 2026-10-07. Caller: Johnathon Ghormley. For businesses with <b>no website</b> (or only Facebook / a free builder address). Package A. Replaces the List A parts of Call Script - Free Design Offer.</i></p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> get a \"yes, build it\" for the <b>free design</b>, and collect what you need to build it. Don't sell the $200. The design sells it.</p>\n<p><b>Before you dial (30 seconds in the CRM):</b> owner's name, trade, city, Abby's <b>Opener</b> (rapport note), and where they show up now (Google listing, Facebook, nothing).</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>1. If someone else answers (main line)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi, this is Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs. I sent a letter to y'all's main location and just wanted to follow up on that with the owner. Is <b>[owner name]</b> around?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"We didn't get a letter.\"</b> → \"Oh, well, you know how it is. Snail mail, sometimes they get lost. Happens all the time.\"</li>\n<li><b>\"What's this about?\"</b> → \"I put together something for <b>[business]</b>, a free website design. Just takes a minute to explain. Is he/she in?\"</li>\n<li><b>Not in</b> → \"No problem. When's the best time to catch them? And is there a better number for them directly?\" Log the time and any number in the CRM.</li>\n<li><b>\"Send an email\"</b> → \"Sure, what's the best email?\" Then still ask: \"When's a good time for me to call back?\"</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Opener</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hey <b>[name]</b>, this is Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs, here in Bay Area Houston. I'll be quick. Did I catch you at an OK time?\"</blockquote>\n<p>Bad time → \"No problem. When's better, later today or tomorrow morning?\" Log the callback.</p>\n<h3>3. Rapport (keep it short, let them talk)</h3>\n<p>Use Abby's opener:</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"I was looking at <b>[business]</b>. I saw <b>[your Google reviews / how long you've been around / that you do ___]</b>. How long have you been doing <b>[trade]</b>?\"</blockquote>\n<p>Follow-up if they're talking:</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"How do most of your new customers find you right now?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>Listen. If they say word of mouth, Google, or Facebook, use it in step 4.</i></p>\n<h3>4. The reason for the call</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"The reason I'm calling: when I searched for <b>[business]</b>, I couldn't find a website. People <b>[heard about you / saw your truck]</b> look you up on their phone before they call. Right now they find <b>[just a Google listing / a Facebook page / someone else]</b>.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>5. The offer</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Here's what I do. I'll build you a <b>free homepage design</b>, your name, your services, your area, a tap-to-call button. No cost, no obligation. You look at it on your phone, and if you don't like it, that's the end of it.<br>If you do like it, it's <b>$200</b> for the site plus a <b>$25</b> setup fee, and I set up your web address in your name, so you own it. Then it's <b>$50 a month</b>. That covers hosting, your web address, an app to manage the site, and you call me directly if anything ever goes wrong.<br>Want me to put one together for you?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>Then stop talking. Let them answer.</i></p>\n<h3>6. If yes: get what you need</h3>\n<ul class=\"check\">\n<li>\"What's the best way to send it, <b>text or email</b>?\"</li>\n<li>\"What are the main jobs you want people to call you for?\"</li>\n<li>\"What areas do you cover?\"</li>\n<li>\"Got a logo you like?\" (Not needed. \"I can design it with your name for now.\")</li>\n<li>\"Any web address you'd like, like <b>[business]</b>.com?\" (Check it's free later.)</li>\n<li>Lock the next call: \"I'll have it to you in <b>2 days</b>. Can I call you <b>[day]</b> around <b>[time]</b> to walk through it?\"</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close: \"Perfect. Talk to you <b>[day]</b>.\" In the CRM: call status <b>Design Sent</b> after Dex builds it; set the follow-up date.</p>\n<h3>7. Objections (List A)</h3>\n<p><b>\"I don't need a website. I get all my work from word of mouth.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"That's the best kind of business. But when someone gets your name from a neighbor, the first thing they do is look you up. A site just makes sure they find you, not the next guy. And the design's free, so it costs nothing to look.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"I've got a Facebook page.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"That's great, keep it. A lot of people don't use Facebook though, and Google ranks a real site higher. I'll link your Facebook right on it.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"I don't have the money right now.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Totally get it. The design is free, so there's nothing to decide today. If you like it, it's $225 to get going, about one service call for most guys, and no long contract.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"How much is it?\"</b> (asked early)</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"$200 for the site and $25 setup, then $50 a month for hosting and support. But I'll build the design first for free so you can see if it's worth it.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"$50 a month is a lot.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"It covers everything: hosting, your web address, changes when you need them, and you call me directly, not a call center. One extra job a month more than pays for it.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"What's the catch? Is this a scam?\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Fair question. No catch, and nothing to pay unless you like it. The web address is registered in your name, so you own it even if you ever leave.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"I'm too busy to deal with a website.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"That's why I do it all for you. I just need 2 minutes now, and you look at the design when it's ready.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"Just send me some info.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Even better, I'll send you the actual design so you can see it. Text or email?\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"Not interested.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"No problem at all. Thanks for your time. Mind if I check back in a few months?\" Log the outcome. If they ask not to be called again, log <b>Asked not to call</b>.</blockquote>\n<h3>8. Voicemail (under 20 seconds)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi <b>[name]</b>, this is Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs. I noticed <b>[business]</b> doesn't have a website yet, and I'd like to build you a free design, no cost, no obligation. Call or text me at <b>832-508-0059</b>. Again, 832-508-0059. Thanks.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>9. Text after a voicemail or no answer</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi [name], Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs. I left you a voicemail. I'd like to build [business] a free website design, no cost or obligation. Want me to put one together? 832-508-0059\"</blockquote>\n<h3>10. Follow-up call (after the design is sent)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hey <b>[name]</b>, it's Johnathon. Did you get a chance to look at the design? What did you think?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Likes it</b> → \"Great. It's $225 to get started, then $50 a month. I'll send the invoice and a simple agreement. Any web address you'd like?\" → CRM: <b>Won</b>, package A.</li>\n<li><b>Wants changes</b> → write them down, have Dex revise, set a new follow-up.</li>\n<li><b>No</b> → \"What would have made it a yes?\" Log the answer.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p><b>Rules:</b> dial by hand, be honest, never promise anything not in Offer &amp; Pricing. Respect \"don't call me\" right away. Log every call in the CRM.</p>", "B": "<p><i>v2.1, 2026-10-08 (letter follow-up gatekeeper opener). v2 2026-10-07. Caller: Johnathon Ghormley. For businesses that <b>already have a website or own a domain</b>. Package B. Replaces the List B parts of Call Script - Free Design Offer.</i></p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> get a \"yes\" to a <b>free side-by-side redesign</b> of their current site. Never trash their site. Show them something better and let them compare.</p>\n<p><b>Before you dial (1 minute):</b> open their site <b>on your phone</b>. Note one or two specific, fair problems from Abby's <b>Website notes</b> (e.g. not mobile friendly, no tap-to-call, copyright 2016, slow, missing services). Also note the owner's name, trade, city, and Abby's <b>Opener</b>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>1. If someone else answers (main line)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi, this is Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs. I sent a letter to y'all's main location and just wanted to follow up on that with the owner. Is <b>[owner name]</b> around?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"We didn't get a letter.\"</b> → \"Oh, well, you know how it is. Snail mail, sometimes they get lost. Happens all the time.\"</li>\n<li><b>\"What's this about?\"</b> → \"It's about the <b>[business]</b> website. I put together an idea for it. Just takes a minute. Is he/she in?\"</li>\n<li><b>\"Our nephew / a company does our website\"</b> → \"No problem, it's just a free idea for them to look at. When's a good time to catch <b>[owner]</b>?\"</li>\n<li><b>Not in</b> → \"When's the best time to reach them? Is there a better number for them directly?\" Log it in the CRM.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Opener</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hey <b>[name]</b>, this is Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs, here in Bay Area Houston. I'll be quick. Did I catch you at an OK time?\"</blockquote>\n<p>Bad time → \"No problem. Later today or tomorrow morning?\" Log the callback.</p>\n<h3>3. Rapport</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"I was looking at <b>[business]</b>. I saw <b>[Abby's opener: reviews / years in business / something specific]</b>. How long have you been at it?\"</blockquote>\n<p>Then:</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Do you get many calls from your website, or is it mostly word of mouth?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>Their answer tells you which angle to use in step 4.</i></p>\n<h3>4. The reason for the call (respectful, specific)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"I pulled up your site on my phone. You've got good info on there. <b>[One specific issue, e.g.: the text is pretty small on a phone / there's no button to tap and call / it looks like it hasn't been updated in a while]</b>. Most people looking for <b>[trade]</b> are on their phone, so that's where it matters most.\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>One issue is enough. Don't list everything wrong.</i></p>\n<h3>5. The offer</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Here's what I do. I'll take what's on your current site and build you a <b>free redesign</b>: same info, your same look and feel, just modern, fast, and easy on a phone. You put them side by side, and if yours is better, no harm done.<br>If you like mine, it's <b>$200</b> one time to switch over, and you <b>keep your same web address</b>. Then it's <b>$50 a month</b> for hosting, an app to manage the site, and you call me directly if anything goes wrong.<br>Want me to put one together?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>Stop talking. Let them answer.</i></p>\n<h3>6. If yes: get what you need</h3>\n<ul class=\"check\">\n<li>\"Text or email for sending it?\"</li>\n<li>\"Anything on your current site that's out of date, or anything you wish it said?\"</li>\n<li>\"Any services you want front and center?\"</li>\n<li>\"Who set up your web address, GoDaddy, Wix, someone you know?\" (Only needed if they buy. Don't push for logins now.)</li>\n<li>Lock the next call: \"I'll have it to you in <b>2 days</b>. Can I call you <b>[day]</b> around <b>[time]</b> to look at it together?\"</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close: \"Perfect, talk to you <b>[day]</b>.\" In the CRM: <b>Design Sent</b> after Dex builds it; set the follow-up date.</p>\n<h3>7. Objections (List B)</h3>\n<p><b>\"I already have a website.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Totally, and I'm not saying throw it away. I'll just build a free version side by side. If yours is better, you've lost nothing.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"My website works fine.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Good to hear. Have you looked at it on your phone lately? That's where most of your customers see it. Let me show you a version built for phones, free, and you decide.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"Someone already handles my website\" (nephew, friend, a company).</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"That's great. This doesn't step on anyone. It's a free idea you can compare. If you like it, you can even show it to them.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"I just paid for my website.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Makes sense. Keep it if it's working. If it's not bringing in calls, the redesign is free to look at, and switching is $200 one time.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"What happens to my domain / email?\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"You keep your same web address, it stays in your name. Your email stays exactly how it is. I just point the address at the new site.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"How much?\"</b> (asked early)</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"$200 one time to switch, then $50 a month for hosting and support. But I build the redesign first, free, so you can see if it's worth it.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"$50 a month is a lot.\" / \"I pay less now.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"What you pay now probably covers hosting only. Mine includes hosting, changes when you need them, an app to manage the site, and my direct number. One extra job a month covers it.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"What's the catch?\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"No catch. Nothing to pay unless you like it, and you keep your web address either way.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"Just send me some info.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Even better, I'll send you the actual redesign. Text or email?\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>\"Not interested.\"</b></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"No problem, thanks for your time. Mind if I check back in a few months?\" Log it. If they ask not to be called, log <b>Asked not to call</b>.</blockquote>\n<h3>8. Voicemail (under 20 seconds)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi <b>[name]</b>, this is Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs. I took a look at the <b>[business]</b> website and I'd like to build you a free modern version to compare, no cost, no obligation. Call or text me at <b>832-508-0059</b>. Again, 832-508-0059. Thanks.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>9. Text after a voicemail or no answer</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi [name], Johnathon with Affordable Web Designs. I left you a voicemail. I'd like to build a free modern redesign of the [business] website for you to compare side by side, no cost. Want me to put one together? 832-508-0059\"</blockquote>\n<h3>10. Follow-up call (after the design is sent)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hey <b>[name]</b>, it's Johnathon. Did you get a chance to compare the new design with your current site? What did you think?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Likes it</b> → \"Great. It's $200 to switch, then $50 a month. I'll send the invoice and a simple agreement. Where's your web address registered?\" → CRM: <b>Won</b>, package B.</li>\n<li><b>Wants changes</b> → note them, have Dex revise, set a new follow-up.</li>\n<li><b>No</b> → \"What would have made it a yes?\" Log the answer.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p><b>Rules:</b> dial by hand, be honest, never criticize their current web person, never promise anything not in Offer &amp; Pricing. Respect \"don't call me\" right away. Log every call in the CRM.</p>"};
